-- title:
--   Constancy of the level-ℓ' Weil pairing on the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$; let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ consisting exactly of the supersingular places $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\ q\ M'$, let $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$, let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ compatible with coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series over $A$ ($h_{R_0}$), and let $s \in W$. Let $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ be an intermediate field and put $A_0 = A \cap k_0$ with residue field $\kappa$; it is assumed that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by some $\pi_0 \in k_0 \cap A$, that $A_0$ is Henselian with $\kappa$ algebraically closed, and that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$. Let $\ell' \ne q$ be a prime with $\ell' \ge 3$ and $\ell' \nmid M'$, let $\xi \in k_0$ be a primitive $q\ell'$-th root of unity admitting a ring embedding $k_0 \to \mathbb C$ sending it to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$, and let $K \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ k_0$ be the base change to $k_0$ of the function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell')^2M'$ with $H = \mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M'$, equipped with an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with $k_0$, together with $j \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the image of $\mathrm{jq}$ and with $j \ne 0$. Further data: the variable-change equivariance hypotheses $h_\ell$ for Katz level-$\ell'$ structures $\mathrm{IsLevelPStructure}$ and $h_M$ for $\mathrm{IsGamma0PowAt}$ under $\mathrm{kernelVariableChangeDeg}$; group laws $\mathcal G$ over $A_0$ that are chord-tangent and origin-preserving; a level transport $\mathcal T$ for $\mathcal G$ and $q$ that is a section transport; and the hypotheses $h_{VC}$, $h_{CO}$ providing graded homomorphisms of projective-model gradings realising variable changes and coefficient maps (each dominating the irrelevant ideal). Let $R = \mathrm{rigidDataPow}\ A_0\ \ell'\ M'\ q\ h_\ell\ h_M\ \mathcal G\ \mathcal T$, let $P_0$ be an abstract level moduli package for $R.\mathrm{toLevelModuliDatum}$, let $x_0$ be a point of that datum over $K$ whose $j$-invariant has Laurent expansion $\mathrm{jqNModC}\ k_0\ (q\ell')$, and let $\mathrm{clC} : P_0.B_0 \to C$ be an $A_0$-algebra map into the chart algebra $C = \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\ A_0\ K\ j$ (elements of $K$ integral over $A_0[j]$) whose composite with the inclusion $C \subseteq K$ is $P_0.\mathrm{classify}\ x_0$. The conclusion asserts the existence of one unit $c \in \kappa^\times$ such that for every maximal ideal $y$ of $C$, every $A_0$-algebra map $\psi : C \to \kappa$ whose vanishing locus is exactly $y$, and every raw datum $x$ for $R$ over $\kappa$ (a Weierstrass curve with unit discriminant together with level data satisfying the level conditions) whose class in $R.\mathrm{Pt}\ \kappa$ equals the image of $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under $\psi \circ \mathrm{clC}$, the Weil pairing $\mathrm{weilPairing0}$ of $x.\mathrm{curve}$ over $\kappa$ at $\ell'$, evaluated on the two points obtained by $\mathrm{LevelRelabelling.toPoint}$ from the coordinates $(x_P,y_P)$ and $(x_Q,y_Q)$ of the Katz level-$\ell'$ component of $x.\mathrm{level}$, equals $c$.
--
--   This is the constancy of the $\ell'$-Weil pairing of the universal Katz level-$\ell'$ basis along the closed points of the special fibre of the rigid level-$q\ell'$ chart: the pairing is an $\ell'$-th root of unity in the coordinate ring, hence a constant of $A_0$, and its residue is therefore independent of the closed point and of the chosen raw representative. It is used by the supersingular fibre dictionary statements for this chart, where a single pairing value must be attached to the whole fibre.
